1
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Rags is a tv movie, comedy, drama film directed by Bille Woodruff.

2
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Rags follows the story of Charlie Prince, an orphan living with his acerbic and
unloving stepfather and spoiled, simple-minded stepbrothers.

3
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Charlie's dream is to be a singer, and while he is vocally talented
and can write music, he can't seem to catch a break.

4
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Kadee Worth, on the other hand, is the daughter of music mogul
Reginald Worth and is an international pop phenomenon.

5
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
While the world knows her as a glamorous superstar, she is secretly frustrated with
singing other people's songs and wearing clothes other people choose for her.

6
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Kadee wants the world to hear and see her true talent.

7
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Despite every obstacle that gets thrown in their way, once Charlie and Kadee find one another, they each
finally get what they have been looking for – a voice, a stage, an audience and each other.

8
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Kadee Worth, played by Keke Palmer.

9
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Charlie Prince, played by Max Schneider.

10
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Reginald Worth, played by Isaiah Mustafa.

11
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Finn, played by Avan Jogia.

12
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Shawn, played by Drake Bell.

13
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Lloyd McGowens, played by Burkely Duffield.

14
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Rags is a Nickelodeon Original Movie.

15
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It is a musical, gender-switched inversion and modernization of the Cinderella fairy tale,
starring Keke Palmer, Max Schneider, Drake Bell, Avan Jogia, and Nick Cannon.

16
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
The film premiered on Nickelodeon on May 28, 2012.

17
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
The film was released on DVD on August 28, 2012, as a
double feature with Big Time Movie.

18
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film explores themes of dreams, competition, musical, singer, teenager.

19
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
